Template: mcprack/public_base_url
Type: string
Priority: medium
Default:
Description: Public base URL of this mcprack instance:
 Enter the externally reachable URL, for example
 https://mcprack.example.com. It is used for password-reset links,
 OAuth metadata and Host validation. Leave empty to configure it later
 in /etc/mcprack/env.

Template: mcprack/gunicorn_bind
Type: string
Priority: low
Default: 127.0.0.1:8912
Description: Address and port where the mcprack web server listens:
 The default listens on the local machine only. Change this only when
 mcprack must accept connections on another interface; expose it through
 a trusted reverse proxy or firewall.

Template: mcprack/oauth_enabled
Type: boolean
Priority: low
Default: false
Description: Enable the OAuth authorization server:
 Enable OAuth authorization for MCP clients. This requires PUBLIC_BASE_URL
 to be set to the externally reachable address. If disabled, clients can
 continue to use aggregate URLs with signed path tokens.

Template: mcprack/session_cookie_secure
Type: boolean
Priority: low
Default: true
Description: Require HTTPS for authentication cookies:
 Leave enabled for internet-facing installations or when TLS is terminated
 by a reverse proxy. Disable only for a trusted intranet served over plain
 HTTP.